From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:10:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] UI/Gtk: Build against the LibWebView API of February
 2026

The GTK frontend was written against the LibWebView of April 2026. This
tree is older, so adapt the frontend to it:

- There are no bookmarks yet: drop the bookmark menu/bar overrides and
  the bookmark and fullscreen media action IDs, the "engaged" action
  state and the submenu group icon.
- Autocomplete results are plain strings, not AutocompleteSuggestion.
- Backing stores are Gfx::Bitmaps rather than SharedImageBuffers.
- Mouse events have no click count; repeated presses are sent as
  DoubleClick/TripleClick events instead, cycling every third press
  like the Qt frontend does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
